<%# The public landing page: five sections.

    It was eleven, and half its visitors never scrolled past the first. What a
    visitor does here, in the order they did it when measured: tap the problem
    in the hero (which was a picture), pick a grade (which was at the very
    bottom), or go to an exam or a competition. So the problem is a real one
    to answer, the grades are on the first screen, and three doors lead to the
    rest of the site. How it works is three lines; the long answer — the phone
    in the child's hands, the rating bands, goals, the duel — is „За родители"
    (static_pages/parents), and the bank in numbers is on /matematika.

    Two rules still hold. The artwork is the product: a real .practice-card
    with real .choice-buttons, no illustrations and no stock photography. And
    every number is a mechanic the app has, read from the constant that
    implements it, so nothing here can drift out of step with the code. There
    is no pricing, no usage metric and no testimonial, because none of the
    three exist yet. %>

<%# --- Hero ---------------------------------------------------------------- %>
<div class="math-hero border-b border-ink-100 pb-10 sm:pb-12">
<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_.95fr] lg:gap-14">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h1 class="landing-h1 mb-4"><%= t("landing.hero.title") %></h1>

      <p class="landing-lede mb-6 max-w-[40ch]">
        <%= t("landing.hero.lede", minutes: DailyPractice::DEFAULT_MINUTES) %>
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 max-sm:flex-col">
        <%= link_to sign_up_path, class: "button button-primary button-hero" do %>
          <%= t("landing.sign_up") %> →
        <% end %>
        <%# A visitor who is not ready to give an email can still see what a
            session is like (TrialsController) — and is asked again at its end. %>
        <%= link_to t("landing.hero.try"), trial_path, class: "button button-secondary button-hero", data: { trace: "trial-open" } %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# One problem to answer, built from the classes the practice flow uses.
        It was a picture of an answered problem, and most of the taps it got
        did nothing; now a tap answers it (sample_choice_controller, as on the
        content pages) and offers the trial. %>
    <div class="landing-peek min-w-0" data-controller="sample-choice">
      <div class="practice-meta">
        <span class="topic-pill"><%= t("landing.peek.topic") %></span>
        <span class="level-label"><%= t("landing.peek.try") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-card p-5 sm:p-6">
        <div class="question-body-large mb-4 flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5">
          <span><%= t("landing.peek.stem_before") %></span>
          <%= math_value("3/4") %>
          <span><%= t("landing.peek.stem_after") %></span>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2.5">
          <% [ 12, 15, 16, 18 ].each do |option| %>
            <%= tag.button option, type: "button", class: "choice-button flex min-h-13 items-center justify-center py-3 text-lg",
                           aria: { pressed: false },
                           data: { sample_choice_target: "option", action: "sample-choice#pick", correct: option == 15, trace: "hero-choice" } %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3.5 text-center text-meta font-extrabold text-ink-600" data-sample-choice-target="hint">
        <%= t("landing.peek.hint") %>
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-[14px] bg-white px-4 py-3 ring-1 ring-ink-200" hidden data-sample-choice-target="more">
        <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 basis-40 text-sm font-bold text-ink-700">
          <span class="block font-black text-ink-900"><%= t("landing.peek.answer") %></span>
          <%= t("landing.peek.why") %>
        </p>
        <%= link_to "#{t("landing.peek.more", count: Trial::LENGTH)} →", trial_path, class: "button button-secondary", data: { trace: "trial-open" } %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# --- The grades -------------------------------------------------------
      The grade pages are where a parent's search lands, and the root page
      linking to them is how a crawler finds them at all. These tiles were the
      page's most-used links from the bottom of it, where one visitor in five
      scrolled. %>
  <div class="mt-10 sm:mt-14">
    <h2 class="landing-eyebrow"><%= t("landing.grades.pick") %></h2>
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2.5 sm:grid-cols-6 lg:grid-cols-12" aria-label="<%= t("landing.nav.grades_label") %>">
      <% Curriculum.grades.each do |grade| %>
        <li>
          <%= link_to curriculum_grade_path(grade.slug), class: "grade-key", aria: { label: grade.name } do %>
            <span class="block text-2xl font-black leading-none text-primary-900"><%= grade.number %></span>
            <span class="block text-micro font-extrabold text-ink-600"><%= t("curriculum.klas") %></span>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <%# One line where there was a strip of four tiles. The bank's count is
        the only figure that is not a constant (BankStats), and below
        BankStats::MINIMUM the minutes stand in for it. %>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-extrabold text-ink-600">
      <% if @bank %>
        <%= t("landing.proof.line_bank", count: number_with_delimiter(BankStats.floor(@bank.total), delimiter: " "),
                                         widgets: Widgets::REGISTRY.size) %>
      <% else %>
        <%= t("landing.proof.line", minutes: DailyPractice::DEFAULT_MINUTES, widgets: Widgets::REGISTRY.size) %>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<%# --- Three doors ----------------------------------------------------------
    People arrive for different reasons — a матура in June, a Kangaroo in
    March, tonight's homework — and each has a section of the site. The exam
    and competition dates are read off the competitions tables, the same ones
    the calendar renders. %>
<section id="zashto" class="landing-section scroll-mt-20">
  <h2 class="landing-h2 mb-6"><%= t("landing.doors.title") %></h2>

  <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <li class="landing-tile flex flex-col pb-2 sm:pb-3">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black tracking-[-.01em]">
        <%= link_to t("landing.intents.exams.title"), exams_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
      </h3>
      <ul class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-ink-100 border-t border-ink-100">
        <% public_exams.each do |exam| %>
          <li>
            <%= link_to exam_page_path(exam.slug), class: "landing-door-row" do %>
              <span><%= exam.name %></span>
              <span><%= round_date(exam.next_round || exam.rounds.last) %></span>
            <% end %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li class="landing-tile flex flex-col pb-2 sm:pb-3">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black tracking-[-.01em]">
        <%= link_to t("landing.intents.competitions.title"), competition_calendar_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
      </h3>
      <ul class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-ink-100 border-t border-ink-100">
        <% @upcoming_competitions.each do |event| %>
          <li>
            <%= link_to competition_page_path(event.slug), class: "landing-door-row" do %>
              <span class="min-w-0 truncate"><%= event.name %></span>
              <span><%= round_date(event.next_round) %></span>
            <% end %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
        <li>
          <%= link_to "#{t("landing.intents.competitions.link")} →", competition_calendar_path, class: "link-cta" %>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li class="landing-tile flex flex-col pb-2 sm:pb-3">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black tracking-[-.01em]"><%= t("landing.doors.tools") %></h3>
      <ul class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-ink-100 border-t border-ink-100">
        <% [
             [ t("curriculum.index.tools.explainers"), t("landing.doors.explainers_count", count: Explainers.all.size), explainers_path ],
             [ t("curriculum.index.tools.formulas"), t("landing.doors.formulas_span"), formulas_path ],
             [ t("curriculum.index.tools.calculators"), t("landing.doors.calculators_count", count: Calculators.all.size), formulas_path(anchor: "kalkulatori") ],
             [ t("curriculum.index.tools.table"), nil, times_table_path ]
           ].each do |title, note, path| %>
          <li>
            <%= link_to path, class: "landing-door-row" do %>
              <span><%= title %></span>
              <% if note %><span><%= note %></span><% end %>
            <% end %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<%# --- How it works, in three lines ------------------------------------------ %>
<section id="how" class="landing-section scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="landing-panel">
    <div class="mb-7 flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-x-10 gap-y-2">
      <h2 class="landing-h2"><%= t("landing.adaptive.title") %></h2>
      <%= link_to "#{t("landing.how.more")} →", for_parents_path,
                  class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-ui font-black text-white hover:underline" %>
    </div>

    <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-10 gap-y-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <% [
           [ t("landing.how.short.find.title", count: Placement::QUESTION_COUNT), t("landing.how.short.find.body") ],
           [ t("landing.how.short.daily.title", minutes: DailyPractice::DEFAULT_MINUTES), t("landing.how.short.daily.body") ],
           [ t("landing.how.short.return.title"), t("landing.how.short.return.body") ]
         ].each_with_index do |(title, body), index| %>
        <li>
          <div class="mb-3.5 grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-white/15 text-base font-black" aria-hidden="true"><%= index + 1 %></div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-black tracking-[-.01em]"><%= title %></h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-ui font-semibold text-primary-100"><%= body %></p>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<%# --- FAQ --------------------------------------------------------------------
    Folded to the questions, with every answer in the HTML: the FAQPage markup
    (StaticPagesController#faq_schema) mirrors exactly these six, from the
    same translation keys. %>
<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px]">
    <h2 class="landing-h2 mb-5"><%= t("landing.faq.title") %></h2>

    <div class="landing-folds">
      <% [
           [ t("landing.faq.age.q"), t("landing.faq.age.a") ],
           [ t("landing.faq.time.q"), t("landing.faq.time.a", minutes: DailyPractice::DEFAULT_MINUTES) ],
           [ t("landing.faq.not_taught.q"), t("landing.faq.not_taught.a", days: AnswerSubmission::DEFERRAL_DAYS) ],
           [ t("landing.faq.authoring.q"), t("landing.faq.authoring.a") ],
           [ t("landing.faq.competitions.q"), t("landing.faq.competitions.a") ],
           [ t("landing.faq.matura.q"), t("landing.faq.matura.a") ]
         ].each do |question, answer| %>
        <details class="landing-fold">
          <summary><%= question %></summary>
          <p class="landing-body max-w-[64ch]"><%= answer %></p>
        </details>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# --- Closing call to action ---------------------------------------------- %>
<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="landing-cta-band">
    <h2 class="landing-h2 mb-3 text-primary-900">
      <%= t("landing.closing.title", minutes: DailyPractice::DEFAULT_MINUTES) %>
    </h2>
    <p class="landing-body mx-auto mb-6 max-w-[52ch] text-primary-800"><%= t("landing.closing.body") %></p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 max-sm:flex-col">
      <%= link_to sign_up_path, class: "button button-primary button-hero" do %>
        <%= t("landing.sign_up") %> →
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to t("landing.closing.secondary"), sign_in_path,
                  class: "button button-hero border border-primary-200 bg-white text-primary-900 hover:bg-primary-25" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
